#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM Quantum Composer is a graphical programming tool. Drag and drop "
"operations to build circuits and run them on quantum hardware."
msgstr ""
"Ang IBM Quantum Composer ay isang graphical na tool sa programming. I-drag "
"and drop ang mga operasyon para gumawa ng mga circuit at patakbuhin ang mga "
"ito sa quantum hardware."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Composer"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Composer"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore gatename, ungroup, ungrouping */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore gatename, ungroup, ungrouping */}\n"

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Composer {#ibm-quantum-composer}"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Composer {#ibm-quantum-composer}"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is it? {#what-is-it}"
msgstr "Ano ito? {#what-is-it}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[IBM Quantum&reg; Composer](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer) is a "
"graphical quantum programming tool that lets you drag and drop operations to"
" build quantum circuits and run them on quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [IBM Quantum&reg; Composer](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer) ay "
"isang graphical na tool sa quantum programming na nagpapahintulot sa iyo na "
"mag-drag and drop ng mga operasyon para gumawa ng mga quantum circuit at "
"patakbuhin ang mga ito sa quantum hardware.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What can it do? {#what-can-it-do}"
msgstr "Ano ang kaya nitong gawin? {#what-can-it-do}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Visualize qubit states**\n"
msgstr "**I-visualize ang mga qubit state**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"See how changes to your circuit affect the state of qubits, shown as an "
"interactive q-sphere, or histograms showing measurement probabilities or "
"statevector simulations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingnan kung paano naapektuhan ng mga pagbabago sa iyong circuit ang estado "
"ng mga qubit, na ipinapakita bilang interactive na q-sphere, o histograms na"
" nagpapakita ng mga probability ng measurement o statevector simulation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Run on quantum hardware**\n"
msgstr "**Patakbuhin sa quantum hardware**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Run your circuits on real quantum hardware to understand the effects of "
"device noise.\n"
msgstr ""
"Patakbuhin ang iyong mga circuit sa totoong quantum hardware para maunawaan "
"ang mga epekto ng device noise.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Automatically generate code**\n"
msgstr "**Awtomatikong gumawa ng code**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Instead of writing code by hand, automatically generate OpenQASM or Python "
"code that behaves the same way as the circuit you created with the "
"Composer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa halip na manual na magsulat ng code, awtomatikong gumawa ng OpenQASM o "
"Python code na katulad ng gawi ng circuit na ginawa mo sa Composer.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Tour of the interface {#tour-of-the-interface}"
msgstr "Pagtingin sa interface {#tour-of-the-interface}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM Quantum Composer has a customizable set of tools that allow you to "
"build, visualize, and run quantum circuits on quantum processing units "
"(QPUs). Use the \"More options\" menu on each window to access additional "
"tools and actions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang IBM Quantum Composer ay may customizable na set ng mga tool na "
"nagpapahintulot sa iyo na bumuo, mag-visualize, at magpatakbo ng mga quantum"
" circuit sa mga quantum processing unit (QPU). Gamitin ang \"More options\" "
"na menu sa bawat window para ma-access ang karagdagang mga tool at aksyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![IBM Quantum Composer window](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-"
"annotation.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![IBM Quantum Composer window](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-"
"annotation.svg)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Operations catalog** - These are the building blocks of quantum circuits. "
"Drag and drop these gates and other operations onto the graphical circuit "
"editor. Different types of gates are grouped together by color. For example,"
" classical gates are dark blue, phase gates are light blue, and non-unitary "
"operations are grey.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Operations catalog** - Ito ang mga building block ng mga quantum circuit. "
"I-drag and drop ang mga gate at iba pang operasyong ito sa graphical circuit"
" editor. Ang iba't ibang uri ng gate ay nakagrupo ayon sa kulay. Halimbawa, "
"ang mga classical gate ay maitim na asul, ang mga phase gate ay maliwanag na"
" asul, at ang mga non-unitary na operasyon ay kulay abo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   To learn about the available gates and operations, right-click an "
"operation and select Info to read its definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Para matuto tungkol sa mga available na gate at operasyon, i-right-click "
"ang isang operasyon at piliin ang Info para basahin ang kahulugan nito.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Code editor** - Use the View menu to open or close the code editor, which "
"allows you to view the OpenQASM or Qiskit code for the circuit. You can edit"
" the OpenQASM code; the Qiskit code is read-only.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Code editor** - Gamitin ang View menu para buksan o isara ang code editor,"
" na nagpapahintulot sa iyo na tingnan ang OpenQASM o Qiskit code para sa "
"circuit. Maaari kang mag-edit ng OpenQASM code; ang Qiskit code ay read-"
"only.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Graphical circuit editor** - This is where you build a circuit. Drag gates"
" and other operations onto the horizontal qubit “wires” that make up your "
"quantum register.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Graphical circuit editor** - Dito mo binubuo ang isang circuit. I-drag ang"
" mga gate at iba pang operasyon sa mga pahalang na qubit \"wire\" na bumubuo"
" ng iyong quantum register.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   To remove a gate from a wire, select the gate and click the trash can "
"icon.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Para alisin ang isang gate mula sa wire, piliin ang gate at i-click ang "
"trash can icon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   To edit the parameters and settings on gates that support editing, select"
" the gate on the graphical editor and click Edit.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Para i-edit ang mga parameter at setting ng mga gate na sinusuportahan "
"ang pag-edit, piliin ang gate sa graphical editor at i-click ang Edit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Toolbar** - Access frequently used tools to undo and redo actions, change "
"the gate alignment, and switch to inspect mode. With inspect mode, you see a"
" step-by-step view of the qubit states as you circuit computation evolves. "
"To learn more, see [Inspect your circuit, step-by-step](#4-inspect-your-"
"circuit-step-by-step).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Toolbar** - I-access ang mga madalas na ginagamit na tool para i-undo at "
"i-redo ang mga aksyon, baguhin ang gate alignment, at lumipat sa inspect "
"mode. Sa inspect mode, makikita mo ang step-by-step na view ng mga qubit "
"state habang umuusad ang computation ng iyong circuit. Para matuto pa, "
"tingnan ang [I-inspect ang iyong circuit, hakbang-hakbang](#4-inspect-your-"
"circuit-step-by-step).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Phase disks** - The phase of the qubit state vector in the complex plane "
"is given by the line that extends from the center of the diagram to the edge"
" of the gray disk (which rotates counterclockwise around the center "
"point).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Phase disks** - Ang phase ng qubit state vector sa complex plane ay "
"ibinibigay ng linya na umaabot mula sa gitna ng diagram patungong gilid ng "
"gray disk (na umiikot counterclockwise sa paligid ng center point).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "    Use the View menu to show or hide the phase disks.\n"
msgstr "    Gamitin ang View menu para ipakita o itago ang mga phase disk.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Visualizations** - Visualizations characterize your circuit as you build "
"it. They use a single-shot statevector simulator, which is different from "
"the QPU specified in the \"Run circuit\" settings. Note that the "
"visualizations ignore any measurement operations you add. Sign in and click "
"**Run circuit** to get results from the specified backend instead.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Visualizations** - Inilalarawan ng mga visualization ang iyong circuit "
"habang ginagawa mo ito. Gumagamit sila ng single-shot statevector simulator,"
" na naiiba sa QPU na tinukoy sa \"Run circuit\" settings. Tandaan na hindi "
"pinapansin ng mga visualization ang anumang measurement operation na "
"idinagdag mo. Mag-sign in at i-click ang **Run circuit** para makuha ang mga"
" resulta mula sa tinukoy na backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   Learn more in the [Visualizations](#visualizations) section.\n"
msgstr "   Matuto pa sa seksyong [Visualizations](#visualizations).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Build, edit, and inspect quantum circuits {#build-edit-and-inspect-quantum-"
"circuits}"
msgstr ""
"Bumuo, mag-edit, at mag-inspect ng mga quantum circuit {#build-edit-and-"
"inspect-quantum-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"warning\" title=\"Download your circuit files before "
"exiting the Composer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"warning\" title=\"I-download ang iyong mga circuit file "
"bago umalis sa Composer\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you want to continue working with a circuit at a later time, be sure to download your circuit file and store it locally before exiting your current Composer session. Use the \"Save file\" link in the upper-right corner, or go to the File menu and choose \"Save file\". When you are ready to work with the circuit again, go to the File menu and choose \"Upload .qasm file\", then navigate to your circuit file on your local drive and click Open.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung gusto mong magpatuloy sa pagtatrabaho sa isang circuit sa ibang pagkakataon, siguraduhing i-download ang iyong circuit file at itago ito nang lokal bago umalis sa iyong kasalukuyang Composer session. Gamitin ang \"Save file\" na link sa kanang sulok sa itaas, o pumunta sa File menu at piliin ang \"Save file\". Kapag handa ka nang magtrabaho muli sa circuit, pumunta sa File menu at piliin ang \"Upload .qasm file\", pagkatapos ay hanapin ang iyong circuit file sa iyong lokal na drive at i-click ang Open.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Open IBM Quantum Composer {#1-open-ibm-quantum-composer}"
msgstr "1. Buksan ang IBM Quantum Composer {#1-open-ibm-quantum-composer}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(Optional) If you are not currently signed in to IBM Quantum, select **Sign "
"in** in the upper right corner. Then, you can either sign in or **Create an "
"IBM Cloud account**.\n"
msgstr ""
"(Opsyonal) Kung hindi ka pa naka-sign in sa IBM Quantum, piliin ang **Sign "
"in** sa kanang sulok sa itaas. Pagkatapos, maaari kang mag-sign in o "
"**Gumawa ng IBM Cloud account**.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   If you don’t sign in, the visualizations automatically show simulated results for up to four qubits. If you want to run your circuit on a quantum computer, or if you want to visualize a circuit that has more than four qubits, you must sign in.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   Kung hindi ka mag-sign in, awtomatikong nagpapakita ng mga simulated na resulta ang mga visualization para sa hanggang apat na qubit. Kung gusto mong patakbuhin ang iyong circuit sa isang quantum computer, o kung gusto mong mag-visualize ng circuit na may higit sa apat na qubit, kailangan mong mag-sign in.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Open IBM Quantum Composer by clicking the link on the [Learning "
"page](/learning) navigation. The workspace displays an untitled empty "
"circuit. You can either create a new circuit, or upload a .qasm file to "
"continue working with with a circuit you've already created. \n"
msgstr ""
"Buksan ang IBM Quantum Composer sa pamamagitan ng pag-click sa link sa "
"[Learning page](/learning) navigation. Ipinapakita ng workspace ang isang "
"walang titulong walang laman na circuit. Maaari kang lumikha ng bagong "
"circuit, o mag-upload ng .qasm file para magpatuloy sa pagtatrabaho sa isang"
" circuit na nagawa mo na.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Name your circuit by clicking on the words **Untitled circuit** and typing "
"in a name for your circuit. Click the checkmark to save the name.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pangalanan ang iyong circuit sa pamamagitan ng pag-click sa mga salitang "
"**Untitled circuit** at pag-type ng pangalan para sa iyong circuit. I-click "
"ang checkmark para i-save ang pangalan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "(Optional) Customize your workspace:\n"
msgstr "(Opsyonal) I-customize ang iyong workspace:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the **View** menu to change from the default theme to a monochrome "
"theme. You can also select which panels to include on your workspace, then "
"use the menu in the right corner of any panel to access options for further "
"customization. The options to show or hide phase disks, choose the alignment"
" of the qubits on your circuit, and reset the workspace to the default are "
"in the View menu as well.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamitin ang **View** menu para magpalit mula sa default na tema patungong "
"monochrome na tema. Maaari ka ring pumili kung aling mga panel ang isasama "
"sa iyong workspace, pagkatapos gamitin ang menu sa kanang sulok ng anumang "
"panel para ma-access ang mga opsyon para sa karagdagang customization. Ang "
"mga opsyon para ipakita o itago ang mga phase disk, pumili ng alignment ng "
"mga qubit sa iyong circuit, at i-reset ang workspace sa default ay nasa View"
" menu rin.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '   * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Switch between dark and light workspace themes in the bottom-right corner of"
" the footer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lumipat sa pagitan ng dark at light na tema ng workspace sa kanang sulok sa "
"ibaba ng footer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To build a circuit, you can either [drag and drop operations](#2-build-your-"
"circuit-with-drag-and-drop), or you can enter [OpenQASM code](#3-build-your-"
"circuit-with-openqasm-code) into the code editor.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para bumuo ng circuit, maaari kang [mag-drag and drop ng mga "
"operasyon](#2-build-your-circuit-with-drag-and-drop), o maaari kang magpasok"
" ng [OpenQASM code](#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code) sa code "
"editor.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2. Build your circuit with drag-and-drop {#2-build-your-circuit-with-drag-"
"and-drop}"
msgstr ""
"2. Bumuo ng iyong circuit gamit ang drag-and-drop {#2-build-your-circuit-"
"with-drag-and-drop}"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Operations catalog {#operations-catalog}"
msgstr "Operations catalog {#operations-catalog}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Drag and drop operations from the operations catalog onto the quantum and "
"classical registers. Click the search icon and enter a term in the search "
"bar to quickly find an operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mag-drag and drop ng mga operasyon mula sa operations catalog papunta sa mga"
" quantum at classical register. I-click ang search icon at magpasok ng "
"termino sa search bar para mabilis na mahanap ang isang operasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Collapse and expand the operations catalog by clicking the icon in the upper"
" right corner of the operations panel. Click the icon next to it to toggle "
"between a grid and list view of the catalog.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-collapse at i-expand ang operations catalog sa pamamagitan ng pag-click sa"
" icon sa kanang sulok sa itaas ng operations panel. I-click ang icon sa tabi"
" nito para lumipat sa pagitan ng grid at list view ng catalog.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Right-click an operation icon and select Info to view the definition of an "
"operation, along with its QASM reference.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-right-click ang isang operation icon at piliin ang Info para tingnan ang "
"kahulugan ng isang operasyon, kasama ang QASM reference nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To undo or redo, use the curved arrows in the toolbar.\n"
msgstr "Para mag-undo o mag-redo, gamitin ang mga curved na arrow sa toolbar.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alignment {#alignment}"
msgstr "Alignment {#alignment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose Freeform alignment to place operations anywhere on the circuit. For a"
" more compact view of your circuit, choose Left alignment. To see the order "
"in which operations will execute, choose Layers alignment, which will apply "
"left alignment and add column delineators that indicate the execution order,"
" from left to right and top to bottom.\n"
msgstr ""
"Piliin ang Freeform alignment para ilagay ang mga operasyon kahit saan sa "
"circuit. Para sa mas compact na view ng iyong circuit, piliin ang Left "
"alignment. Para makita ang pagkakasunod-sunod ng pagpapatupad ng mga "
"operasyon, piliin ang Layers alignment, na mag-a-apply ng left alignment at "
"magdadagdag ng mga column delineator na nagpapahiwatig ng pagkakasunod-sunod"
" ng pagpapatupad, mula kaliwa hanggang kanan at mula itaas hanggang ibaba.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once operations are placed on your circuit, you can continue to drag and "
"drop them to new positions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nakalagay na ang mga operasyon sa iyong circuit, maaari kang "
"magpatuloy na mag-drag and drop ng mga ito sa mga bagong posisyon.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Copy and paste {#copy-and-paste}"
msgstr "Copy at paste {#copy-and-paste}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Click an operation and use the icons in the contextual menu to copy and "
"paste it.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-click ang isang operasyon at gamitin ang mga icon sa contextual menu para "
"kopyahin at i-paste ito.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Select multiple operations {#select-multiple-operations}"
msgstr "Pumili ng maraming operasyon {#select-multiple-operations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can select several operations to copy and paste them, drag them to a new"
" location, or group them into a custom unitary operation that displays in "
"your operations catalog and functions as a single gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari kang pumili ng ilang operasyon para kopyahin at i-paste ang mga ito, "
"i-drag ang mga ito sa bagong lokasyon, o i-group ang mga ito sa isang custom"
" na unitary operation na lumalabas sa iyong operations catalog at gumagana "
"bilang isang solong gate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To select more than one operation, place your cursor just outside one of the"
" operations, then click and drag across the area to select. Shift-click "
"individual operations to select or deselect them. A dashed line outlines the"
" set of operations you are selecting, and each operation that is actually "
"part of the selection is outlined in blue.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para pumili ng higit sa isang operasyon, ilagay ang iyong cursor sa labas "
"lamang ng isa sa mga operasyon, pagkatapos i-click at i-drag sa buong lugar "
"para pumili. Shift-click ang mga indibidwal na operasyon para piliin o "
"alisin ang mga ito sa pagpili. Ang isang may katiting na linya ay "
"nagbabalangkas sa set ng mga operasyong pinipili mo, at ang bawat operasyong"
" aktwal na bahagi ng pagpili ay nakabalangkas sa asul.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, in the following image, the Hadamard gate on q1 and the CX gate"
" are selected. The Hadamard gate on q0 is not selected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa, sa sumusunod na larawan, ang Hadamard gate sa q1 at ang CX gate "
"ay napili. Ang Hadamard gate sa q0 ay hindi napili.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A set of selected "
"operations](/docs/images/guides/composer/3c5c063d-b15f-43cb-"
"bb65-9728187454d8.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A set of selected "
"operations](/docs/images/guides/composer/3c5c063d-b15f-43cb-"
"bb65-9728187454d8.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Select Copy from the contextual menu to copy the group.\n"
msgstr "Piliin ang Copy mula sa contextual menu para kopyahin ang grupo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To paste the group of operations, right-click in the circuit and select "
"Paste.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para i-paste ang grupo ng mga operasyon, i-right-click sa circuit at piliin "
"ang Paste.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Build a custom operation using the group feature {#build-a-custom-operation-"
"using-the-group-feature}"
msgstr ""
"Bumuo ng custom na operasyon gamit ang group feature {#build-a-custom-"
"operation-using-the-group-feature}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To group several operations together and save them as a custom operation, "
"first select the operations as described above, then select Group from the "
"contextual menu. You are prompted to name the custom operation or you can "
"accept the default name. Click OK, and the custom operation will be "
"represented by a single box, both in your circuit and in the operations "
"catalog.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para i-group ang ilang operasyon at i-save ang mga ito bilang custom na "
"operasyon, una ay piliin ang mga operasyon gaya ng inilarawan sa itaas, "
"pagkatapos piliin ang Group mula sa contextual menu. Ipo-prompt kang "
"pangalanan ang custom na operasyon o maaari kang tanggapin ang default na "
"pangalan. I-click ang OK, at ang custom na operasyon ay itatakda ng isang "
"solong kahon, kapwa sa iyong circuit at sa operations catalog.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can now drag and drop the new operation throughout your circuit. Note "
"that the operation is saved to this circuit but does not appear in the "
"operations catalog for other circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mo na ngayong i-drag and drop ang bagong operasyon sa buong iyong "
"circuit. Tandaan na ang operasyon ay nai-save sa circuit na ito ngunit hindi"
" lumalabas sa operations catalog para sa ibang mga circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can also build a custom operation directly in the OpenQASM code editor; "
"see [Create a custom operation in OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-"
"openqasm) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari ka ring bumuo ng custom na operasyon nang direkta sa OpenQASM code "
"editor; tingnan ang [Gumawa ng custom na operasyon sa OpenQASM](#create-a-"
"custom-operation-in-openqasm) para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ungroup a custom or predefined operation {#ungroup-a-custom-or-predefined-"
"operation}"
msgstr ""
"I-ungroup ang isang custom o predefined na operasyon {#ungroup-a-custom-or-"
"predefined-operation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To ungroup the gates within a custom or predefined operation, click the "
"operation on the Composer and select Ungroup from the contextual menu. You "
"can now move the separate operations individually. When you ungroup an "
"operation, each element in the former group executes independently, which "
"may mean they execute in a different order from when they were grouped "
"together.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para i-ungroup ang mga gate sa loob ng isang custom o predefined na "
"operasyon, i-click ang operasyon sa Composer at piliin ang Ungroup mula sa "
"contextual menu. Maaari mo na ngayong ilipat ang mga hiwalay na operasyon "
"nang isa-isa. Kapag na-ungroup mo ang isang operasyon, ang bawat elemento sa"
" dating grupo ay nagpapatupad nang nakapag-iisa, na maaaring mangahulugang "
"nagpapatupad sila sa ibang pagkakasunod-sunod kaysa nang nagrupo sila.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Expand an operation’s definition {#expand-an-operations-definition}"
msgstr ""
"I-expand ang kahulugan ng isang operasyon {#expand-an-operations-definition}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To view the operations that constitute a custom or predefined operation "
"without ungrouping them, click **Expand definition** from the contextual "
"menu to see the defining gates. Click the icon again to collapse the "
"definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para tingnan ang mga operasyong bumubuo sa isang custom o predefined na "
"operasyon nang hindi ini-ungroup ang mga ito, i-click ang **Expand "
"definition** mula sa contextual menu para makita ang mga defining gate. "
"I-click muli ang icon para i-collapse ang kahulugan.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Rename or delete a custom operation {#rename-or-delete-a-custom-operation}"
msgstr ""
"Palitan ng pangalan o burahin ang isang custom na operasyon {#rename-or-"
"delete-a-custom-operation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To rename or delete a custom operation, right-click the operation in the "
"operations catalog and select Rename or Delete. Deleting a custom operation "
"from the operations catalog also deletes any instances of it on your "
"circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para palitan ng pangalan o burahin ang isang custom na operasyon, i-right-"
"click ang operasyon sa operations catalog at piliin ang Rename o Delete. Ang"
" pagbubura ng custom na operasyon mula sa operations catalog ay nagtatanggal"
" din ng anumang instance nito sa iyong circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deleting a custom operation from the circuit itself does not delete it from "
"the operations catalog; you can only delete a custom operation from the "
"catalog by using right-click and selecting Delete.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagbubura ng custom na operasyon mula sa circuit mismo ay hindi ito "
"binubura mula sa operations catalog; maaari mo lamang burahin ang custom na "
"operasyon mula sa catalog sa pamamagitan ng right-click at pagpili ng "
"Delete.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add or remove registers {#add-or-remove-registers}"
msgstr "Magdagdag o mag-alis ng mga register {#add-or-remove-registers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To add or remove quantum or classical registers, click Edit → Manage "
"registers. You can increase or decrease the number of qubits or bits in your"
" circuit and rename the registers. Click **Ok** to apply the changes. You "
"can also simply click the register name (e.g., `q[0]`) and use the options "
"in the contextual menu to quickly add or delete registers or qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para magdagdag o mag-alis ng mga quantum o classical register, i-click ang "
"Edit → Manage registers. Maaari mong dagdagan o bawasan ang bilang ng mga "
"qubit o bit sa iyong circuit at palitan ng pangalan ang mga register. "
"I-click ang **Ok** para ilapat ang mga pagbabago. Maaari ka ring i-click "
"lamang ang pangalan ng register (hal., `q[0]`) at gamitin ang mga opsyon sa "
"contextual menu para mabilis na magdagdag o magtanggal ng mga register o "
"qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add a conditional {#add-a-conditional}"
msgstr "Magdagdag ng conditional {#add-a-conditional}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To add a conditional to a gate, drag the `if` operation to the gate and set "
"the parameters in the Edit operation panel that automatically opens. You can"
" also double-click a gate to access the Edit operation panel, and set the "
"conditional parameters that way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para magdagdag ng conditional sa isang gate, i-drag ang operasyong `if` sa "
"gate at itakda ang mga parameter sa Edit operation panel na awtomatikong "
"bubukas. Maaari ka ring mag-double-click ng isang gate para ma-access ang "
"Edit operation panel, at itakda ang mga conditional parameter sa ganitong "
"paraan.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add a control modifier {#add-a-control-modifier}"
msgstr "Magdagdag ng control modifier {#add-a-control-modifier}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A control modifier yields a gate whose original operation is now contingent "
"on the state of the control qubit. For more details, right-click the control"
" modifier symbol in the operations catalog, then click Info.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang control modifier ay nagbubunga ng isang gate na ang orihinal na "
"operasyon ay nakasalalay na ngayon sa estado ng control qubit. Para sa "
"karagdagang detalye, i-right-click ang control modifier symbol sa operations"
" catalog, pagkatapos i-click ang Info.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Drag the control modifier to a gate in order to add a control to it. A dot "
"appears on the control qubit and a line connects it to the target qubit. To "
"edit which qubit is the control or target, click the gate and select the "
"Edit operation icon (or double-click the gate) to open the Edit operation "
"panel, then specify your parameters. From the Edit operation panel, you can "
"also remove a control from a qubit by clicking the x next to the qubit "
"name.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-drag ang control modifier sa isang gate para magdagdag ng control dito. "
"Lumalabas ang isang tuldok sa control qubit at isang linya ang kumukonekta "
"nito sa target qubit. Para i-edit kung aling qubit ang control o target, "
"i-click ang gate at piliin ang Edit operation icon (o i-double-click ang "
"gate) para buksan ang Edit operation panel, pagkatapos tukuyin ang iyong mga"
" parameter. Mula sa Edit operation panel, maaari ka ring mag-alis ng control"
" mula sa isang qubit sa pamamagitan ng pag-click sa x sa tabi ng pangalan ng"
" qubit.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Visualize with phase disks throughout your circuit {#visualize-with-phase-"
"disks-throughout-your-circuit}"
msgstr ""
"I-visualize gamit ang mga phase disk sa buong iyong circuit {#visualize-"
"with-phase-disks-throughout-your-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To visualize the state of all qubits at any point in your circuit, drag the "
"phase disk icon from the operations catalog and place it anywhere in your "
"circuit. A column of barrier operations and a column of phase disks are "
"added (one barrier operation and phase disk per qubit). Hover over each "
"phase disk to read the state of the qubit at that point in the circuit. Note"
" that adding the phase disks does not alter your circuit; they are merely a "
"visualization tool.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ma-visualize ang estado ng lahat ng qubit sa anumang punto ng iyong "
"circuit, i-drag ang phase disk icon mula sa operations catalog at ilagay ito"
" kahit saan sa iyong circuit. Isang column ng mga barrier operation at isang"
" column ng mga phase disk ang idinaragdag (isang barrier operation at phase "
"disk bawat qubit). Mag-hover sa bawat phase disk para mabasa ang estado ng "
"qubit sa puntong iyon sa circuit. Tandaan na ang pagdaragdag ng mga phase "
"disk ay hindi nagbabago ng iyong circuit; mga visualization tool lamang "
"sila.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Read more about the [phase disk visualization](#phase-disk).\n"
msgstr "Magbasa pa tungkol sa [phase disk visualization](#phase-disk).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Export a circuit image {#export-a-circuit-image}"
msgstr "Mag-export ng circuit image {#export-a-circuit-image}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To export an image of your circuit, select File → Export circuit image. The "
"Export options window opens, where you can choose a theme (light, dark, "
"white on black, or black on white), a format (.svg or .png), and whether you"
" want to apply a line wrap. After you’ve chosen your options, click "
"Export.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para mag-export ng larawan ng iyong circuit, piliin ang File → Export "
"circuit image. Bubukas ang Export options window, kung saan maaari kang "
"pumili ng tema (light, dark, white on black, o black on white), isang format"
" (.svg o .png), at kung gusto mong mag-apply ng line wrap. Pagkatapos mapili"
" ang iyong mga opsyon, i-click ang Export.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3. Build your circuit with OpenQASM code {#3-build-your-circuit-with-"
"openqasm-code}"
msgstr ""
"3. Bumuo ng iyong circuit gamit ang OpenQASM code {#3-build-your-circuit-"
"with-openqasm-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"IBM Quantum Composer currently supports OpenQASM 2.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Kasalukuyang sinusuportahan ng IBM Quantum Composer ang OpenQASM 2.0.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To open the code editor, click View → Panels → Code Editor.\n"
msgstr "Para buksan ang code editor, i-click ang View → Panels → Code Editor.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"See the [Composer operations glossary](#composer-operations-glossary) for "
"OpenQASM references to gates and other operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingnan ang [Composer operations glossary](#composer-operations-glossary) "
"para sa mga OpenQASM reference sa mga gate at iba pang operasyon.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can define your own custom operations; see [Create a custom operation in"
" OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm).\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari kang mag-define ng sarili mong custom na operasyon; tingnan ang "
"[Gumawa ng custom na operasyon sa OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-"
"openqasm).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For more information on using the OpenQASM language, including sample lines "
"of code, see the [Introduction to OpenQASM](/guides/introduction-to-qasm) "
"guide, or read the original research paper, [Open Quantum Assembly "
"Language](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429). The "
"[table](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=9) of OpenQASM language "
"statements from the paper is reproduced below. The OpenQASM grammar can be "
"found in [Appendix A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21) of the "
"paper.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa karagdagang impormasyon sa paggamit ng OpenQASM language, kasama ang"
" mga sample na linya ng code, tingnan ang gabay na [Panimula sa "
"OpenQASM](/guides/introduction-to-qasm), o basahin ang orihinal na research "
"paper, [Open Quantum Assembly Language](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429). "
"Ang [talahanayan](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=9) ng mga "
"OpenQASM language statement mula sa papel ay muling inilathala sa ibaba. Ang"
" OpenQASM grammar ay matatagpuan sa [Appendix "
"A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21) ng papel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<p></p>\n"
"<table width=\"100%\">\n"
"<thead>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<th>Statement</th>\n"
"<th>Description</th>\n"
"<th>Example</th>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</thead>\n"
"<tbody><tr>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Denotes a file in OpenQASM format (see [a])</td>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>qreg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare a named register of qubits</td>\n"
"<td><code>qreg q[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>creg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare a named register of bits</td>\n"
"<td><code>creg c[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>include “filename”;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Open and parse another source file</td>\n"
"<td><code>include “qelib1.inc”;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gate name(params) qargs</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare a unitary gate</td>\n"
"<td>(see text of paper)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>opaque name(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Declare an opaque gate</td>\n"
"<td>(see text of paper)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>// comment text</code></td>\n"
"<td>Comment a line of text</td>\n"
"<td><code>// oops!</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>U(theta,phi,lambda) qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Apply built-in single-qubit gate(s) (see [b])</td>\n"
"<td><code>U(pi/2,2\\*pi/3,0) q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>CX qubit|qreg,qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Apply built-in CNOT gate(s)</td>\n"
"<td><code>CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>measure qubit|qreg -&gt; bit|creg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Make measurement(s) in $Z$ basis</td>\n"
"<td><code>measure q -&gt; c;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>reset qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Prepare qubit(s) in $\\vert 0\\rangle$</td>\n"
"<td><code>reset q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gatename(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Apply a user-defined unitary gate</td>\n"
"<td><code>crz(pi/2) q[1],q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>if(creg==int) qop;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Conditionally apply quantum operation</td>\n"
"<td><code>if(c==5) CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>barrier qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Prevent transformations across this source line</td>\n"
"<td><code>barrier q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</tbody></table>\n"
msgstr ""
"<p></p>\n"
"<table width=\"100%\">\n"
"<thead>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<th>Statement</th>\n"
"<th>Paglalarawan</th>\n"
"<th>Halimbawa</th>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</thead>\n"
"<tbody><tr>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Nagtatanda ng file sa OpenQASM format (tingnan ang [a])</td>\n"
"<td><code>OPENQASM 2.0;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>qreg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Mag-declare ng named na register ng mga qubit</td>\n"
"<td><code>qreg q[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>creg name[size];</code></td>\n"
"<td>Mag-declare ng named na register ng mga bit</td>\n"
"<td><code>creg c[5];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>include \"filename\";</code></td>\n"
"<td>Buksan at i-parse ang isa pang source file</td>\n"
"<td><code>include \"qelib1.inc\";</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gate name(params) qargs</code></td>\n"
"<td>Mag-declare ng unitary gate</td>\n"
"<td>(tingnan ang teksto ng papel)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>opaque name(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Mag-declare ng opaque gate</td>\n"
"<td>(tingnan ang teksto ng papel)</td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>// comment text</code></td>\n"
"<td>Mag-comment ng isang linya ng teksto</td>\n"
"<td><code>// oops!</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>U(theta,phi,lambda) qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Mag-apply ng built-in na single-qubit gate (tingnan ang [b])</td>\n"
"<td><code>U(pi/2,2\\*pi/3,0) q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>CX qubit|qreg,qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Mag-apply ng built-in na CNOT gate</td>\n"
"<td><code>CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>measure qubit|qreg -&gt; bit|creg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Gumawa ng measurement sa $Z$ basis</td>\n"
"<td><code>measure q -&gt; c;</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>reset qubit|qreg;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Ihanda ang qubit sa $\\vert 0\\rangle$</td>\n"
"<td><code>reset q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>gatename(params) qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Mag-apply ng user-defined na unitary gate</td>\n"
"<td><code>crz(pi/2) q[1],q[0];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>if(creg==int) qop;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Kondisyonal na mag-apply ng quantum operation</td>\n"
"<td><code>if(c==5) CX q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"<tr>\n"
"<td><code>barrier qargs;</code></td>\n"
"<td>Pigilan ang mga transformation sa linya ng source na ito</td>\n"
"<td><code>barrier q[0],q[1];</code></td>\n"
"</tr>\n"
"</tbody></table>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "\\[a] This must appear as the first non-comment line of the file.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\[a] Kailangan itong lumabas bilang unang non-comment na linya ng file.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\[b] The parameters theta, phi, and lambda are given by *parameter "
"expressions*; for more information, see [page 5 of the "
"paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429#page=5) and [Appendix "
"A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21).\n"
msgstr ""
"\\[b] Ang mga parameter na theta, phi, at lambda ay ibinibigay ng mga "
"*parameter expression*; para sa karagdagang impormasyon, tingnan ang [pahina"
" 5 ng papel](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429#page=5) at [Appendix "
"A](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.03429.pdf#page=21).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create a custom operation in OpenQASM {#create-a-custom-operation-in-"
"openqasm}"
msgstr ""
"Gumawa ng custom na operasyon sa OpenQASM {#create-a-custom-operation-in-"
"openqasm}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can define new unitary operations in the code editor (see the figure "
"below for an example). The operations are applied using the statement "
"`name(params) qargs;` just like the built-in operations. The parentheses are"
" optional if there are no parameters.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari kang mag-define ng mga bagong unitary operation sa code editor "
"(tingnan ang figure sa ibaba para sa halimbawa). Ang mga operasyon ay "
"inaaplayan gamit ang statement na `name(params) qargs;` tulad ng mga built-"
"in na operasyon. Ang mga panaklong ay opsyonal kung walang parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To define a custom operation, enter it in the OpenQASM code editor using "
"this format: `gatename(params) qargs;`. If you click **+Add** in the "
"operations list, you will be prompted to enter a name for your custom "
"operation, which you can then build in the code editor.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para mag-define ng custom na operasyon, ipasok ito sa OpenQASM code editor "
"gamit ang format na ito: `gatename(params) qargs;`. Kung i-click mo ang "
"**+Add** sa listahan ng mga operasyon, ipo-prompt kang magpasok ng pangalan "
"para sa iyong custom na operasyon, na maaari mo itong buuin sa code "
"editor.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once you have defined your custom operation, drag it onto the graphical "
"editor and use the edit icon to fine-tune the parameters.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag na-define mo na ang iyong custom na operasyon, i-drag ito sa graphical"
" editor at gamitin ang edit icon para i-fine-tune ang mga parameter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Example of a custom operation | |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| The gates to be included in the custom operation: | ![Gates in the custom operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/763d3b42-4b6e-4409-817f-7d15abae2d76.avif)|\n"
"| The code for the new operation: | ![Customized new operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/db5856ca-751c-4f12-9f25-6060b9003687.avif) | \n"
"| The new operation in the graphical editor: | ![New operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/d7fb8ec5-5eae-4ad4-9972-1e3665b39b7f.avif) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Halimbawa ng custom na operasyon | |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| Ang mga gate na isasama sa custom na operasyon: | ![gates in the custom operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/763d3b42-4b6e-4409-817f-7d15abae2d76.avif)|\n"
"| Ang code para sa bagong operasyon: | ![Customized new operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/db5856ca-751c-4f12-9f25-6060b9003687.avif) |\n"
"| Ang bagong operasyon sa graphical editor: | ![New operation](/docs/images/guides/composer/d7fb8ec5-5eae-4ad4-9972-1e3665b39b7f.avif) |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"4. Inspect your circuit, step-by-step {#4-inspect-your-circuit-step-by-step}"
msgstr ""
"4. I-inspect ang iyong circuit, hakbang-hakbang {#4-inspect-your-circuit-"
"step-by-step}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Inspect mode de-mystifies the inner workings of the circuits you create. It "
"steps through a simulation of your circuit, one layer at a time, so that you"
" can see the state of the qubits as the computation evolves.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Inspect mode ay nagpapaliwanag ng panloob na gawi ng mga circuit na "
"ginagawa mo. Isinasagawa nito ang isang simulation ng iyong circuit, isang "
"layer sa isang pagkakataon, para makita mo ang estado ng mga qubit habang "
"umuusad ang computation.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the **View** menu, select the panels for the visualizations that you want"
" to use.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa **View** menu, piliin ang mga panel para sa mga visualization na gusto "
"mong gamitin.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Click the **Inspect** toggle in the toolbar. Note that once Inspect mode is "
"toggled on, you cannot add any more operations until it is turned off "
"again.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-click ang **Inspect** toggle sa toolbar. Tandaan na kapag na-toggle na ang"
" Inspect mode, hindi ka na maaaring magdagdag ng anumang operasyon hanggang "
"hindi ito naka-off.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you built your circuit with the Freeform alignment turned on, note that "
"Inspect mode automatically turns on the Left alignment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ginawa mo ang iyong circuit nang naka-on ang Freeform alignment, "
"tandaan na awtomatikong sine-switch ng Inspect mode ang Left alignment.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To move step-by-step through visualizations of your circuit’s components, "
"use the forward and rewind buttons.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para lumipat nang hakbang-hakbang sa mga visualization ng mga bahagi ng "
"iyong circuit, gamitin ang mga forward at rewind button.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Controls to step forward and backward, and to jump to a circuit's "
"beginning or "
"end.](/docs/images/guides/composer/5f2dfb7c-a244-405c-8950-f422a4408fcf.avif"
" \"Inspect mode controls, in order: jump to the beginning of a circuit, step"
" backward, play from one break point to the next, step forward, jump to the "
"end of a circuit.\")\n"
msgstr ""
"![Controls to step forward and backward, and to jump to a circuit's "
"beginning or "
"end.](/docs/images/guides/composer/5f2dfb7c-a244-405c-8950-f422a4408fcf.avif"
" \"Inspect mode controls, in order: jump to the beginning of a circuit, step"
" backward, play from one break point to the next, step forward, jump to the "
"end of a circuit.\")\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To inspect only some operations, click the operations you want to be "
"inspected, and a colored overlay appears over each that indicates they will "
"be included when you run in Inspect mode. To unselect an operation, click on"
" it again, and the overlay disappears.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para mag-inspect ng ilang operasyon lamang, i-click ang mga operasyong gusto"
" mong ma-inspect, at isang may kulay na overlay ang lumalabas sa bawat isa "
"na nagpapahiwatig na isasama ang mga ito kapag nagpatakbo sa Inspect mode. "
"Para alisin sa pagpili ang isang operasyon, i-click ito muli, at mawawala "
"ang overlay.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To learn more about interpreting visualizations, see the "
"[Visualizations](#visualizations) topic.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para matuto pa tungkol sa pag-interpret ng mga visualization, tingnan ang "
"paksa na [Visualizations](#visualizations).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To exit Inspect mode and return to editing your circuit, click the Inspect "
"toggle in the toolbar.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para lumabas sa Inspect mode at bumalik sa pag-edit ng iyong circuit, "
"i-click ang Inspect toggle sa toolbar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Randomness in the simulator\">\n"
"The simulator creates randomness by generating results based on a *seed*. The seed is the initial value introduced into the algorithm that generates pseudorandom numbers. You can see the seed number by selecting \"Visualizations seed\" from the Edit menu. You can also set the seed yourself by changing the value in the box.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Randomness sa simulator\">\n"
"Ang simulator ay gumagawa ng randomness sa pamamagitan ng pagbuo ng mga resulta batay sa isang *seed*. Ang seed ay ang paunang halaga na ipinakilala sa algorithm na gumagawa ng mga pseudorandom na numero. Makikita mo ang seed number sa pamamagitan ng pagpili ng \"Visualizations seed\" mula sa Edit menu. Maaari ka ring magtakda ng seed mismo sa pamamagitan ng pagbabago ng halaga sa kahon.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run circuits and view results {#run-circuits-and-view-results}"
msgstr ""
"I-run ang mga circuit at Tingnan ang mga Resulta {#run-circuits-and-view-"
"results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Follow the steps below to run quantum circuits on QPUs and view the "
"results.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sundin ang mga hakbang sa ibaba para i-run ang mga quantum circuit sa QPUs "
"at tingnan ang mga resulta.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose your job settings {#choose-your-job-settings}"
msgstr "Piliin ang mga Setting ng Iyong Job {#choose-your-job-settings}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Click **Run circuit** in the upper right corner. In the window that opens, "
"select an available QPU. You can also choose an instance, which is "
"associated with a plan (such as the Open, Flex, or Premium Plans). The "
"instance you choose affects which QPUs are available to you. Click the "
"\"View details\" link in the table of QPUs to see more information on each "
"QPU.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-click ang **Run circuit** sa kanang sulok sa itaas. Sa window na "
"magbubukas, pumili ng available na QPU. Maaari ka ring pumili ng instance, "
"na nauugnay sa isang plano (tulad ng Open, Flex, o Premium Plans). Ang "
"instance na pipiliin mo ay makakaapekto sa kung aling mga QPU ang available "
"sa iyo. I-click ang link na \"View details\" sa talahanayan ng mga QPU para "
"makita ang karagdagang impormasyon sa bawat QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, you can set the number of shots (executions) of your circuit that the "
"backend will perform.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, maaari mong itakda ang bilang ng mga shot (execution) ng iyong "
"circuit na gagawin ng backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can optionally name the job and add tags in this panel as well. This "
"will not change the name of the circuit. A pre-populated \"Composer\" tag "
"makes it easier to filter your Workloads table by Composer jobs. You can "
"remove this tag.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari ka ring pangalanan ang job at magdagdag ng mga tag sa panel na ito. "
"Hindi nito mababago ang pangalan ng circuit. Ang pre-populated na tag na "
"\"Composer\" ay nagpapadali sa pag-filter ng iyong Workloads table ayon sa "
"mga Composer job. Maaari mong alisin ang tag na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Window displaying job options.](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-"
"run.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Window na nagpapakita ng mga opsyon ng "
"job.](/docs/images/guides/composer/composer-run.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"When you run a circuit, it is automatically sent to the least-busy QPU, unless you specify a QPU in the Run settings. If you run the same circuit again, the QPU selection window will default to your previous choice.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Kapag nag-run ka ng circuit, awtomatiko itong ipinapadala sa pinaka-hindi-abalang QPU, maliban kung tinukoy mo ang isang QPU sa mga Run setting. Kung i-run mo ulit ang parehong circuit, ang window ng pagpili ng QPU ay magde-default sa iyong nakaraang pinili.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Click \"Run on (QPU name)\" {#click-run-on-qpu-name}"
msgstr "I-click ang \"Run on (QPU name)\" {#click-run-on-qpu-name}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can view the job’s progress by clicking the \"View jobs\" button in the "
"top-right corner, which will open the Workloads page in IBM Quantum "
"Platform.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong tingnan ang progreso ng job sa pamamagitan ng pag-click sa "
"button na \"View jobs\" sa kanang sulok sa itaas, na magbubukas ng Workloads"
" page sa IBM Quantum Platform.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "View results {#view-results}"
msgstr "Tingnan ang mga Resulta {#view-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once your job completes, the details are updated in the Workloads table in "
"IBM Quantum Platform.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nakumpleto na ang iyong job, naa-update ang mga detalye sa Workloads "
"table sa IBM Quantum Platform.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Jobs results page displays run details, diagrams of the original and the"
" transpiled circuit, a histogram of the results, and OpenQASM and Qiskit "
"tabs to view both original and transpiled circuits in OpenQASM or Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Jobs results page ay nagpapakita ng mga detalye ng run, mga diagram ng "
"orihinal at ng transpiled na circuit, isang histogram ng mga resulta, at mga"
" tab ng OpenQASM at Qiskit para tingnan ang parehong orihinal at transpiled "
"na mga circuit sa OpenQASM o Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can download the circuits and the histogram by clicking the menu in the "
"upper right corner of each diagram, then selecting a format for the download"
" (PNG, PDF, or SVG; additionally, you can export the histogram as a CSV "
"file). You can open the OpenQASM circuits directly in Composer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong i-download ang mga circuit at ang histogram sa pamamagitan ng "
"pag-click sa menu sa kanang sulok sa itaas ng bawat diagram, pagkatapos ay "
"pumili ng format para sa pag-download (PNG, PDF, o SVG; bukod pa rito, "
"maaari mong i-export ang histogram bilang CSV file). Maaari mong direktang "
"buksan ang mga OpenQASM circuit sa Composer.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Visualizations {#visualizations}"
msgstr "Mga Visualization {#visualizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The live visualizations in IBM Quantum Composer show you different views of "
"how quantum circuits affect the state of a collection of qubits. Each type "
"of live visualization is explained in detail below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga live visualization sa IBM Quantum Composer ay nagpapakita sa iyo ng "
"iba't ibang view kung paano nakakaapekto ang mga quantum circuit sa estado "
"ng isang koleksyon ng mga qubit. Ang bawat uri ng live visualization ay "
"inipaliwanag nang detalyado sa ibaba.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Randomness in the simulator\">\n"
"The live visualizations come from a single-shot statevector simulator, which is different from the QPU specified in the Run settings, which can have multiple shots. The simulator creates randomness by generating results based on a *seed*. The seed is the initial value introduced into the algorithm that generates pseudorandom numbers. You can see the seed number by selecting \"Visualizations seed\" from the Edit menu. You can also set the seed yourself by changing the value in the box.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Randomness sa simulator\">\n"
"Ang mga live visualization ay nagmumula sa isang single-shot statevector simulator, na iba sa QPU na tinukoy sa mga Run setting, na maaaring magkaroon ng maraming shot. Ang simulator ay lumilikha ng randomness sa pamamagitan ng pagbuo ng mga resulta batay sa isang *seed*. Ang seed ay ang paunang halaga na ipinakilala sa algorithm na bumubuo ng mga pseudorandom na numero. Maaari mong makita ang seed number sa pamamagitan ng pagpili ng \"Visualizations seed\" mula sa Edit menu. Maaari mo ring itakda ang seed mismo sa pamamagitan ng pagbabago ng halaga sa kahon.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "View visualizations {#view-visualizations}"
msgstr "Tingnan ang mga Visualization {#view-visualizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The live visualizations are shown in windows at the bottom of the Composer "
"workspace (except the phase disk, which appears at the end of each qubit "
"wire). You can choose any combination of statevector, probabilities, and "
"q-sphere visualizations to appear at the bottom of the workspace. Select or "
"unselect visualizations in the **View** menu.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga live visualization ay ipinapakita sa mga window sa ibaba ng Composer"
" workspace (maliban sa phase disk, na lumalabas sa dulo ng bawat qubit "
"wire). Maaari kang pumili ng anumang kombinasyon ng mga statevector, "
"probabilities, at q-sphere visualization para lumabas sa ibaba ng workspace."
" Pumili o huwag pumili ng mga visualization sa **View** menu.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Download visualizations {#download-visualizations}"
msgstr "I-download ang mga Visualization {#download-visualizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Download one of the visualizations at the bottom of the Composer workspace "
"by clicking the \"More options\" menu in the visualization window. You can "
"download visualizations as an SVG, a PNG, or a CSV of the underlying data. "
"You can also download the visualization images of the measurement "
"probabilities and statevector histograms as a PDF.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-download ang isa sa mga visualization sa ibaba ng Composer workspace sa "
"pamamagitan ng pag-click sa menu na \"More options\" sa visualization "
"window. Maaari mong i-download ang mga visualization bilang SVG, PNG, o CSV "
"ng pinagbabatayan na data. Maaari mo ring i-download ang mga visualization "
"na larawan ng measurement probabilities at statevector histogram bilang "
"PDF.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Phase disk {#phase-disk}"
msgstr "Phase Disk {#phase-disk}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A single-qubit state can be represented as\n"
msgstr "Ang estado ng isang qubit ay maaaring irepresenta bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0\\rangle + e^{j\\varphi} \\sqrt{p} \\vert1\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0\\rangle + e^{j\\varphi} \\sqrt{p} \\vert1\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $p$ is the probability that the qubit is in the $|1\\rangle$ state, "
"and $\\varphi$ is the quantum phase. $p$ is strongly analogous to a "
"classical probabilistic bit. For $p=0$, the qubit is in the $|0\\rangle$ "
"state, for $p=1$ the qubit is in the $|1\\rangle$ state, and for $p=1/2$ the"
" qubit is a 50/50 mixture. We call this a superposition as, unlike classical"
" bits, this mixture can have a quantum phase. The phase disk visualizes this"
" state.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $p$ ay ang probabilidad na ang qubit ay nasa estado ng "
"$|1\\rangle$, at ang $\\varphi$ ay ang quantum phase. Ang $p$ ay halos "
"katulad ng isang klasikal na probabilistic bit. Para sa $p=0$, ang qubit ay "
"nasa $|0\\rangle$ na estado; para sa $p=1$ ang qubit ay nasa $|1\\rangle$ na"
" estado; at para sa $p=1/2$ ang qubit ay isang 50/50 na pinaghalong estado. "
"Tinatawag nating superposition ito dahil, hindi tulad ng mga klasikal na "
"bit, ang pinaghalong ito ay maaaring magkaroon ng quantum phase. Ang phase "
"disk ay nagbibiswal ng estado na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The phase disk at the terminus of each qubit in IBM Quantum Composer gives "
"the local state of each qubit at the end of the computation. The components "
"of the phase disk are described below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang phase disk sa dulo ng bawat qubit sa IBM Quantum Composer ay nagbibigay "
"ng lokal na estado ng bawat qubit sa katapusan ng computation. Ang mga "
"bahagi ng phase disk ay inilarawan sa ibaba.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Probability the qubit is in the** $|1\\rangle$ **state**\n"
msgstr "**Probabilidad na ang qubit ay nasa** $|1\\rangle$ **na estado**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The probability that the qubit is in the $|1\\rangle$ state is represented "
"by the blue disk fill.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang probabilidad na ang qubit ay nasa $|1\\rangle$ na estado ay kinakatawan "
"ng asul na disk fill.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![probability the qubit is in the 1 "
"state](/docs/images/guides/composer/3e4140c6-9da0-46b0-85e4-a1509078d3e9.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![probabilidad na ang qubit ay nasa 1 na "
"estado](/docs/images/guides/composer/3e4140c6-9da0-46b0-85e4-a1509078d3e9.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Quantum phase**\n"
msgstr "**Quantum Phase**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The quantum phase of the qubit state is given by the line that extends from "
"the center of the diagram to the edge of the gray disk (which rotates "
"counterclockwise around the center point).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang quantum phase ng estado ng qubit ay ibinibigay ng linya na umaabot mula "
"sa gitna ng diagram hanggang sa gilid ng gray na disk (na umiikot nang "
"kontra sa orasan sa paligid ng sentral na punto).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![phase of the local qubit "
"state](/docs/images/guides/composer/7f047fde-c19e-46db-b596-be5da55e697e.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![phase ng lokal na estado ng "
"qubit](/docs/images/guides/composer/7f047fde-c19e-46db-b596-be5da55e697e.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Example: phase disks for two different qubits**\n"
msgstr "**Halimbawa: mga phase disk para sa dalawang magkaibang qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![phase disk "
"examples](/docs/images/guides/composer/0207fba8-8b4b-4611-9638-6cbe169e10c4.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![mga halimbawa ng phase "
"disk](/docs/images/guides/composer/0207fba8-8b4b-4611-9638-6cbe169e10c4.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two examples of the phase disk visualization. The first example is a "
"$|1\\rangle$ state and the second shows the "
"$(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$ state with a nonzero relative phase.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalawang halimbawa ng phase disk visualization. Ang unang halimbawa ay isang"
" $|1\\rangle$ na estado at ang pangalawa ay nagpapakita ng "
"$(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$ na estado na may hindi-zero na "
"relatibong phase.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Connection to the Bloch sphere**\n"
msgstr "**Koneksyon sa Bloch Sphere**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The phase disk, which contains all the information in the Bloch sphere, is a"
" two-dimensional representation of a qubit. To convert to the Bloch sphere "
"representation: $x=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Re}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, "
"$y=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Im}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, and $z=1-2p$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang phase disk, na naglalaman ng lahat ng impormasyon sa Bloch sphere, ay "
"isang dalawang-dimensiyonal na representasyon ng isang qubit. Para mag-"
"convert sa Bloch sphere representation: "
"$x=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Re}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, "
"$y=2\\sqrt{p(1-p)}\\mathrm{Im}[e^{j\\varphi} ]$, at $z=1-2p$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**N-qubit states: maximum 15 qubits**\n"
msgstr "**Mga N-qubit na estado: maximum na 15 qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "An N-qubit quantum state takes the form\n"
msgstr "Ang isang N-qubit na quantum state ay may sumusunod na anyo\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0...0\\rangle + \\sum_{k=1}^{2^N-1}e^{j\\varphi_k} \\sqrt{p_k} \\vert k\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{split}\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{1-p}\\vert0...0\\rangle + \\sum_{k=1}^{2^N-1}e^{j\\varphi_k} \\sqrt{p_k} \\vert k\\rangle,\\end{split}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $p_k$ is the probability that the qubits are in the state $|k\\rangle$"
" with quantum phase $\\varphi_k$ with respect to the $|0...0\\rangle$ state."
" $p=\\sum_{k\\neq0}p_k$ is the probability that the qubits are not in the "
"ground state $|0...0\\rangle$. Here it is simple to see that for an N-qubit "
"quantum state there are $2^N-1$ probabilities and $2^N-1$ phases. The phase "
"disk fails to represent this state, as N-qubit phase disks would only "
"contain $N$ probabilities and $N$ phases; this is because most states are "
"entangled and are not separable into independent single-qubit quantum "
"states. To represent that full information is not contained in this "
"visualization, we introduce the reduced purity as a component in the phase "
"disk.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $p_k$ ay ang probabilidad na ang mga qubit ay nasa estado ng "
"$|k\\rangle$ na may quantum phase na $\\varphi_k$ kaugnay ng "
"$|0...0\\rangle$ na estado. Ang $p=\\sum_{k\\neq0}p_k$ ay ang probabilidad "
"na ang mga qubit ay wala sa ground state na $|0...0\\rangle$. Dito ay "
"madaling makita na para sa isang N-qubit na quantum state, mayroong $2^N-1$ "
"na mga probabilidad at $2^N-1$ na mga phase. Nabibigo ang phase disk na "
"irepresenta ang estadong ito, dahil ang N-qubit na mga phase disk ay "
"maglalaman lamang ng $N$ na mga probabilidad at $N$ na mga phase; ito ay "
"dahil karamihan sa mga estado ay entangled at hindi maaaring ihiwalay sa mga"
" independiyenteng single-qubit na quantum state. Para ipakita na ang buong "
"impormasyon ay hindi nilalaman sa visualization na ito, ipinapakilala natin "
"ang reduced purity bilang isang bahagi sa phase disk.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Reduced purity of the qubit state**\n"
msgstr "**Reduced Purity ng estado ng qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The radius of the black ring on the phase disk represents the reduced purity"
" of the qubit state, which for qubit $j$ in an $N$-qubit state "
"$|\\psi\\rangle$ is given by $\\mathrm{Tr}\\left[\\mathrm{Tr}_{i\\neq "
"j}[\\left|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\right|\\right]^{2}]$. The reduced "
"purity for a single qubit is in the range $[0.5, 1]$; a value of one "
"indicates that the qubit is not entangled with any other party. In contrast,"
" a reduced purity of $0.5$ shows that the qubit is left in the completely "
"mixed state, and has some level of entanglement over the remaining $N-1$ "
"qubits, and possibly even the environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang radius ng itim na singsing sa phase disk ay kumakatawan sa reduced "
"purity ng estado ng qubit, na para sa qubit $j$ sa isang $N$-qubit na estado"
" $|\\psi\\rangle$ ay ibinibigay ng $\\mathrm{Tr}\\left[\\mathrm{Tr}_{i\\neq "
"j}[\\left|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\right|\\right]^{2}]$. Ang reduced "
"purity para sa isang solong qubit ay nasa hanay ng $[0.5, 1]$; ang halagang "
"isa ay nagpapahiwatig na ang qubit ay hindi entangled sa anumang ibang "
"partido. Sa kabilang banda, ang reduced purity na $0.5$ ay nagpapakita na "
"ang qubit ay naiwan sa completely mixed state, at may ilang antas ng "
"entanglement sa natitirang $N-1$ na mga qubit, at posibleng maging sa "
"kapaligiran pa.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilities view {#probabilities-view}"
msgstr "Probabilities View {#probabilities-view}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**8-qubit limit**\n"
msgstr "**Limitasyon sa 8 qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This view visualizes the probabilities of the quantum state as a bar graph. "
"The horizontal axis labels the computational basis states. The vertical axis"
" measures the probabilities in terms of percentages. In this view the "
"quantum phases are not represented, and is therefore an incomplete "
"representation. However, it is useful for predicting the outcomes if each "
"qubit is measured and the value stored in its own classical bit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang view na ito ay nagbibiswal ng mga probabilidad ng quantum state bilang "
"isang bar graph. Ang pahalang na axis ay nag-lalabel ng mga computational "
"basis state. Ang patayo na axis ay sumusukat ng mga probabilidad sa "
"pamamagitan ng mga porsyento. Sa view na ito, ang mga quantum phase ay hindi"
" kinakatawan, kaya ito ay isang hindi kumpletong representasyon. Gayunpaman,"
" ito ay kapaki-pakinabang para hulaan ang mga resulta kung ang bawat qubit "
"ay sinusukat at ang halaga ay iniimbak sa sarili nitong klasikal na bit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the following quantum circuit and its probabilities view:\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang ang sumusunod na quantum circuit at ang nito probabilities "
"view:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![a quantum circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg \"A circuit"
" consisting of a column of Hadamards that creates an equal superposition of "
"the computational basis states, followed by a two-qubit controlled-Z (CZ) "
"gate.\")\n"
msgstr ""
"![isang quantum circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg \"Isang"
" circuit na binubuo ng isang kolum ng mga Hadamard na lumilikha ng pantay na"
" superposition ng mga computational basis state, na sinusundan ng isang two-"
"qubit controlled-Z (CZ) gate.\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Probabilities view of the previous "
"circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/probabilities.svg \"Probabilities view"
" of the previous circuit.\")\n"
msgstr ""
"![Probabilities view ng nakaraang "
"circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/probabilities.svg \"Probabilities view"
" ng nakaraang circuit.\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit puts the two qubits into the state $|\\psi\\rangle = "
"(|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2$. The computational"
" basis states are $|00\\rangle, |10\\rangle, |01\\rangle$, and "
"$|11\\rangle$. The probabilities for each of the computational states is "
"1/4.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inilalapat ng circuit ang dalawang qubit sa estado na $|\\psi\\rangle = "
"(|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2$. Ang mga "
"computational basis state ay $|00\\rangle, |10\\rangle, |01\\rangle$, at "
"$|11\\rangle$. Ang mga probabilidad para sa bawat computational state ay "
"1/4.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Q-sphere view {#q-sphere-view}"
msgstr "Q-sphere View {#q-sphere-view}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**5-qubit limit**\n"
msgstr "**Limitasyon sa 5 qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The q-sphere represents the state of a system of one or more qubits by "
"associating each computational basis state with a point on the surface of a "
"sphere. A node is visible at each point. Each node’s radius is proportional "
"to the probability ($p_k$) of its basis state, whereas the node color "
"indicates the quantum phase ($\\varphi_k$).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang q-sphere ay kumakatawan sa estado ng isang sistema ng isa o higit pang "
"qubit sa pamamagitan ng pag-uugnay ng bawat computational basis state sa "
"isang punto sa ibabaw ng isang sphere. Isang node ang nakikita sa bawat "
"punto. Ang radius ng bawat node ay proporsyonal sa probabilidad ($p_k$) ng "
"nito basis state, samantalang ang kulay ng node ay nagpapahiwatig ng quantum"
" phase ($\\varphi_k$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The nodes are laid out on the q-sphere so that the basis state with all "
"zeros (e.g., $|000\\rangle)$ is at its north pole, and the basis state with "
"all ones (e.g., $|111\\rangle$) is at its south pole. Basis states with the "
"same number of zeros (or ones) lie on a shared latitude of the q-sphere "
"(e.g., $|001\\rangle, |010\\rangle, |100\\rangle$). Beginning at the north "
"pole of the q-sphere and progressing southward, each successive latitude has"
" basis states with a greater number of ones; the latitude of a basis state "
"is determined by its [Hamming "
"distance](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamming_distance) from the zero "
"state. The q-sphere contains complete information about the quantum state in"
" a compact representation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga node ay nakalatag sa q-sphere upang ang basis state na may lahat ng "
"sero (hal., $|000\\rangle)$ ay nasa hilagang poste nito, at ang basis state "
"na may lahat ng isa (hal., $|111\\rangle$) ay nasa timog na poste nito. Ang "
"mga basis state na may parehong bilang ng sero (o isa) ay nasa iisang "
"latitude ng q-sphere (hal., $|001\\rangle, |010\\rangle, |100\\rangle$). "
"Simula sa hilagang poste ng q-sphere at patungo sa timog, ang bawat sunod na"
" latitude ay may mga basis state na may mas maraming isa; ang latitude ng "
"isang basis state ay tinutukoy ng nito [Hamming "
"distance](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamming_distance) mula sa zero "
"state. Ang q-sphere ay naglalaman ng kumpletong impormasyon tungkol sa "
"quantum state sa isang compact na representasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the following quantum circuit and its q-sphere, which represent the"
" state the circuit creates:\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang ang sumusunod na quantum circuit at ang nito q-sphere, na "
"kumakatawan sa estado na nililikha ng circuit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![a quantum circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![isang quantum circuit](/docs/images/guides/composer/2H-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "![q-sphere view](/docs/images/guides/composer/q-sphere.avif)\n"
msgstr "![q-sphere view](/docs/images/guides/composer/q-sphere.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can select, hold, and drag to rotate the q-sphere. To return the "
"q-sphere to its default orientation, select the **rewind-arrow button** to "
"the top right of the q-sphere.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari kang pumili, humawak, at mag-drag para i-rotate ang q-sphere. Para "
"ibalik ang q-sphere sa default na oryentasyon nito, piliin ang **rewind-"
"arrow button** sa kanang itaas ng q-sphere.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"What is the difference between a Bloch sphere and a q-sphere?\">\n"
"It is important to highlight that the q-sphere is **not** the same as the Bloch sphere, even for a single qubit. Indeed, like the [phase disk](#phase-disk), the Bloch sphere gives a *local* view of the quantum state, where each qubit is viewed on its own. When trying to understand how registers of qubits (multi-qubit states) behave upon the application of quantum circuits, it is more insightful to take a *global* view and look at the quantum state in its entirety. The q-sphere provides a visual representation of the quantum state, and thus this *global* viewpoint. Therefore, when exploring quantum applications and algorithms on small numbers of qubits, the q-sphere should be the primary visualization method.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Ano ang pagkakaiba ng Bloch sphere at q-sphere?\">\n"
"Mahalaga na i-highlight na ang q-sphere ay **hindi** kapareho ng Bloch sphere, kahit para sa isang solong qubit. Katunayan, tulad ng [phase disk](#phase-disk), ang Bloch sphere ay nagbibigay ng *lokal* na view ng quantum state, kung saan ang bawat qubit ay tinitingnan nang mag-isa. Kapag sinusubukang maunawaan kung paano kumikilos ang mga rehistro ng mga qubit (multi-qubit na estado) sa paglalapat ng mga quantum circuit, mas kapaki-pakinabang na kumuha ng *global* na view at tingnan ang quantum state sa kabuuan nito. Ang q-sphere ay nagbibigay ng visual na representasyon ng quantum state, at kaya naman ang *global* na pananaw na ito. Kaya naman, kapag nag-eeksplora ng mga quantum application at algorithm sa maliit na bilang ng mga qubit, ang q-sphere ang dapat na pangunahing paraan ng visualization.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Statevector view {#statevector-view}"
msgstr "Statevector View {#statevector-view}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**6-qubit limit**\n"
msgstr "**Limitasyon sa 6 na qubit**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is common to call $\\sqrt{p_k}e^{i\\varphi_k}$ the quantum amplitude. "
"This view visualizes the quantum amplitudes as a bar graph. The horizontal "
"axis labels the computational basis states. The vertical axis measures the "
"magnitude of the amplitudes ($\\sqrt{p_k}$) associated with each "
"computational basis state. The color of each bar represents the quantum "
"phase (${\\varphi_k}$).\n"
msgstr ""
"Karaniwan na tinatawag ang $\\sqrt{p_k}e^{i\\varphi_k}$ bilang quantum "
"amplitude. Ang view na ito ay nagbibiswal ng mga quantum amplitude bilang "
"isang bar graph. Ang pahalang na axis ay nag-lalabel ng mga computational "
"basis state. Ang patayo na axis ay sumusukat ng magnitude ng mga amplitude "
"($\\sqrt{p_k}$) na nauugnay sa bawat computational basis state. Ang kulay ng"
" bawat bar ay kumakatawan sa quantum phase (${\\varphi_k}$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the following quantum circuit and its statevector view:\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang ang sumusunod na quantum circuit at ang nito statevector "
"view:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![statevector view](/docs/images/guides/composer/state-vector.svg \"The "
"statevector at the terminus of the above circuit. The color wheel maps phase"
" angle to color. The output state is expressed as a list of complex "
"numbers.\")\n"
msgstr ""
"![statevector view](/docs/images/guides/composer/state-vector.svg \"Ang "
"statevector sa dulo ng circuit sa itaas. Ang color wheel ay nagma-map ng "
"phase angle sa kulay. Ang output state ay ipinahayag bilang isang listahan "
"ng mga kumplikadong numero.\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit puts the two qubits into the state $|\\psi\\rangle = "
"(|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2$. The computational"
" basis states are $|00\\rangle$, $|10\\rangle$, $|01\\rangle$, and "
"$|11\\rangle$. The magnitudes of the amplitudes are $1/2$, and the quantum "
"phases with respect to the ground state are $0$ for $|01\\rangle$ and "
"$|10\\rangle$, and $\\pi$ for $|11\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inilalapat ng circuit ang dalawang qubit sa estado na $|\\psi\\rangle = "
"(|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle+ |10\\rangle-|11\\rangle) / 2$. Ang mga "
"computational basis state ay $|00\\rangle$, $|10\\rangle$, $|01\\rangle$, at"
" $|11\\rangle$. Ang mga magnitude ng amplitude ay $1/2$, at ang mga quantum "
"phase kaugnay ng ground state ay $0$ para sa $|01\\rangle$ at $|10\\rangle$,"
" at $\\pi$ para sa $|11\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Composer operations glossary {#composer-operations-glossary}"
msgstr ""
"Talasalitaan ng mga Operasyon sa Composer {#composer-operations-glossary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This page is a reference that defines the various classical and quantum "
"operations you can use to manipulate qubits in a quantum circuit. Quantum "
"operations include quantum gates, such as the Hadamard gate, as well as "
"operations that are not quantum gates, such as the measurement operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pahinang ito ay isang sanggunian na nagbibigay ng kahulugan sa iba't "
"ibang klasikal at quantum na operasyon na maaari mong gamitin para "
"manipulahin ang mga qubit sa isang quantum circuit. Kabilang sa mga quantum "
"operation ang mga quantum gate, tulad ng Hadamard gate, pati na rin ang mga "
"operasyon na hindi quantum gate, tulad ng measurement operation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each entry below provides details and the OpenQASM reference for each "
"operation. See the topic on [Build your circuit with OpenQASM "
"code](#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code) for more information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bawat entry sa ibaba ay nagbibigay ng mga detalye at ng OpenQASM "
"reference para sa bawat operasyon. Tingnan ang paksa sa [Buuin ang iyong "
"circuit gamit ang OpenQASM code](#3-build-your-circuit-with-openqasm-code) "
"para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The q-sphere image in each gate entry below shows the state after the gate "
"operates on the initial equal superposition state "
"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}|i\\rangle$, where $n$ is the "
"number of qubits needed to support the gate. See the [q-sphere](#q-sphere-"
"view) topic for more information on this visualization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang larawan ng q-sphere sa bawat gate entry sa ibaba ay nagpapakita ng "
"estado pagkatapos maisagawa ng gate ang paunang pantay na superposition "
"state na $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}|i\\rangle$, kung "
"saan ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng mga qubit na kinakailangan para suportahan ang"
" gate. Tingnan ang paksa ng [q-sphere](#q-sphere-view) para sa karagdagang "
"impormasyon sa visualization na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can define a custom operation to use in IBM Quantum Composer. For "
"instructions, see the [Create a custom operation in OpenQASM](#create-a-"
"custom-operation-in-openqasm) topic.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari kang gumawa ng custom na operasyon para gamitin sa IBM Quantum "
"Composer. Para sa mga tagubilin, tingnan ang paksa sa [Gumawa ng custom na "
"operasyon sa OpenQASM](#create-a-custom-operation-in-openqasm).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Gate colors\">\n"
"The gate colors are slightly different in the light and dark themes. The colors from the light theme are shown here.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Mga kulay ng gate\">\n"
"Ang mga kulay ng gate ay bahagyang naiiba sa light at dark theme. Ang mga kulay mula sa light theme ang ipinapakita dito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Click a quantum operation below to view its definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mag-click ng quantum operation sa ibaba para tingnan ang kahulugan nito.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical gates {#classical-gates}"
msgstr "Mga Klasikal na gate {#classical-gates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**NOT Gate**\n"
msgstr "**NOT gate**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The NOT gate, also known as the Pauli X gate, flips the "
"$\\left|0\\right\\rangle$ state to $\\left|1\\right\\rangle$, and vice "
"versa. The NOT gate is equivalent to RX for the angle $\\pi$ or to ‘HZH’.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang NOT gate, na kilala rin bilang Pauli X gate, ay nagba-flip ng estado ng "
"$\\left|0\\right\\rangle$ sa $\\left|1\\right\\rangle$, at vice versa. Ang "
"NOT gate ay katumbas ng RX para sa angle na $\\pi$ o sa 'HZH'.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Composer reference                                | OpenQASM reference | Q-sphere | Note about q-sphere representations                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![x\\_gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/1d52e1a3-ca53-4caa-9700-259e35f0dbaf.avif) | `x q[0];`          | ![image19](/docs/images/guides/composer/1392cb96-3d66-4a9e-9ed1-687a937bc3cc.avif)                              | The q-sphere representation shows the state after the gate operates on the initial equal superposition state $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ where $n$ is the number of qubits needed to support the gate. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Sanggunian sa Composer                                | Sanggunian sa OpenQASM | Q-sphere | Tala tungkol sa mga representasyon ng q-sphere                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![x\\_gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/1d52e1a3-ca53-4caa-9700-259e35f0dbaf.avif) | `x q[0];`          | ![image19](/docs/images/guides/composer/1392cb96-3d66-4a9e-9ed1-687a937bc3cc.avif)                              | Ang representasyon ng q-sphere ay nagpapakita ng estado pagkatapos maisagawa ng gate ang paunang pantay na superposition state na $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ kung saan ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng mga qubit na kinakailangan para suportahan ang gate. |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**CNOT Gate**\n"
msgstr "**CNOT gate**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The controlled-NOT gate, also known as the controlled-x (CX) gate, acts on a"
" pair of qubits, with one acting as ‘control’ and the other as ‘target’. It "
"performs a NOT on the target whenever the control is in state "
"$\\left|1\\right\\rangle$. If the control qubit is in a superposition, this "
"gate creates entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang controlled-NOT gate, na kilala rin bilang controlled-x (CX) gate, ay "
"kumikilos sa isang pares ng mga qubit, na may isa bilang 'control' at ang "
"isa pa bilang 'target'. Nagsasagawa ito ng NOT sa target kapag ang control "
"ay nasa estado ng $\\left|1\\right\\rangle$. Kung ang control qubit ay nasa "
"superposition, ang gate na ito ay lumilikha ng entanglement.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All unitary circuits can be decomposed into single qubit gates and CNOT "
"gates. Because the two-qubit CNOT gate costs much more time to execute on "
"real hardware than single qubit gates, circuit cost is sometimes measured in"
" the number of CNOT gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang lahat ng unitary circuit ay maaaring mabuo mula sa mga single qubit gate"
" at CNOT gate. Dahil ang two-qubit CNOT gate ay mas matagal na i-execute sa "
"tunay na hardware kumpara sa mga single qubit gate, ang gastos ng circuit ay"
" minsan sinusukat sa bilang ng mga CNOT gate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Composer reference                                | OpenQASM reference | Q-sphere | Note about q-sphere representations                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![CX-Gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/e74dca0d-3f6b-42c9-9471-b65fd03ef5b5.avif) | `cx q[0], q[1];`          | ![image19](/docs/images/guides/composer/40abd3fa-ab1e-4ea2-ade7-49a06073b37f.avif)                              | The q-sphere representation shows the state after the gate operates on the initial equal superposition state $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ where $n$ is the number of qubits needed to support the gate. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Sanggunian sa Composer                                | Sanggunian sa OpenQASM | Q-sphere | Tala tungkol sa mga representasyon ng q-sphere                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![CX-Gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/e74dca0d-3f6b-42c9-9471-b65fd03ef5b5.avif) | `cx q[0], q[1];`          | ![image19](/docs/images/guides/composer/40abd3fa-ab1e-4ea2-ade7-49a06073b37f.avif)                              | Ang representasyon ng q-sphere ay nagpapakita ng estado pagkatapos maisagawa ng gate ang paunang pantay na superposition state na $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ kung saan ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng mga qubit na kinakailangan para suportahan ang gate. |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Toffoli gate**\n"
msgstr "**Toffoli gate**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Toffoli gate, also known as the double controlled-NOT gate (CCX), has "
"two control qubits and one target. It applies a NOT to the target only when "
"both controls are in state $\\left|1\\right\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Toffoli gate, na kilala rin bilang double controlled-NOT gate (CCX), ay "
"may dalawang control qubit at isang target. Inilalapat nito ang NOT sa "
"target lamang kapag ang parehong control ay nasa estado ng "
"$\\left|1\\right\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Toffoli gate with the Hadamard gate is a universal gate set for quantum "
"computing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Toffoli gate na may Hadamard gate ay isang universal gate set para sa "
"quantum computing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Composer reference                                    | OpenQASM reference      | Q-sphere | Note about q-sphere representations                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![ccx-gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/16a28c9a-fd2c-4e1b-a0d7-27059adc0aa0.avif) | `ccx q[0], q[1], q[2];` | ![ccx\\_qsph](/docs/images/guides/composer/dc2fb919-f576-4a76-acbe-69dec221145a.avif)                          | The q-sphere representation shows the state after the gate operates on the initial equal superposition state $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ where $n$ is the number of qubits needed to support the gate. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Sanggunian sa Composer                                    | Sanggunian sa OpenQASM      | Q-sphere | Tala tungkol sa mga representasyon ng q-sphere                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![ccx-gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/16a28c9a-fd2c-4e1b-a0d7-27059adc0aa0.avif) | `ccx q[0], q[1], q[2];` | ![ccx\\_qsph](/docs/images/guides/composer/dc2fb919-f576-4a76-acbe-69dec221145a.avif)                          | Ang representasyon ng q-sphere ay nagpapakita ng estado pagkatapos maisagawa ng gate ang paunang pantay na superposition state na $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ kung saan ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng mga qubit na kinakailangan para suportahan ang gate. |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**SWAP gate**\n"
msgstr "**SWAP gate**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The SWAP gate swaps the states of two qubits.\n"
msgstr "Ang SWAP gate ay nagpapalit ng mga estado ng dalawang qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Composer reference                                  | OpenQASM reference | Q-sphere | Note about q-sphere representations                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![SWAP gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/61f641e0-fb8f-4a67-af60-9b1bf792f2c6.avif) | `swap q[0], q[1];` | ![swap\\_qsph](/docs/images/guides/composer/e2090577-7a13-484a-a642-2c56f42119cb.avif)                        | The q-sphere representation shows the state after the gate operates on the initial equal superposition state $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ where $n$ is the number of qubits needed to support the gate. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Sanggunian sa Composer                                  | Sanggunian sa OpenQASM | Q-sphere | Tala tungkol sa mga representasyon ng q-sphere                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
